# Every compositional element of BPMN this emission withholds, and the ground the claim about the
# composition axis stands on despite it. One row per withholding, and exactly one of the two
# grounds is filled.
#
# Why this relation exists
#   A law could not tell two withholdings apart. `diagrams/notation.sqlc`'s ceded law reads a
#   withheld element on the composition axis as a gap in the one axis this model claims whole,
#   which is right when nothing covers the fact and wrong when a better element does: `subProcess`
#   is withheld because `childLaneSet` carries what it would have carried.
#
# The axis is whole for a stated reason
#   The claim is not that every compositional element is spent; it is that every compositional fact
#   is covered. An element may sit in the withheld column only when a spent one carries what it
#   would have carried, and naming which one turns that from an excuse into a sentence that can be
#   checked.
#
# The replacement must itself be spent
#   Otherwise this relation would turn a gap into a citation. That is the part of the law worth
#   probing, not the existence of the row.
#
# The second ground is the boundary claim shrinking
#   It is not an excuse; it is the boundary claim getting weaker and saying so. `no_such_fact`
#   means BPMN offers a compositional element this model has nothing to put in, which is not a gap
#   in this coverage: it is the place where BPMN is the wider of the two. The law admits it and the
#   report counts it, because "on composition this model is the finer" is a claim that has to be
#   allowed to shrink. Moving such a row onto another axis to make the law pass would be
#   reclassifying BPMN to protect a sentence.
#
# Exactly one ground is filled
#   Exactly one of `superseded_by` and `no_such_fact` is filled, the schema's own `<>` idiom. A row
#   with both would be saying the fact is carried and does not exist.
#
# A `VALUES` literal
#   For the reason `diagrams/graphs.sqlc` is one: worked out from the emission, it could only ever
#   report replacements that were carried out correctly, and never a row somebody wrote down and did
#   not carry out.
-- the mapping's own history: what was tried, what replaced it, and where BPMN is simply wider.
SELECT * FROM (VALUES
  ('subProcess'::text, 'childLaneSet'::text, NULL::boolean,
   'A local fusion divides its composed layer among its parts; it is not an activity. '
   '`subProcess` is a flow node, so it collapses layer to document exactly as `calledElement` '
   'does; a nested lane keeps the key `(filing, layer)`'::text),
  ('partitionElementRef', NULL, true,
   'The only place BPMN is the finer of the two. `tLane` carries this for what the lanes are '
   'divided by, per lane. The nearest filler is the absorber buffer, and it does not fit: '
   'several layers of one filing can share one buffer, so pointing at it would assert a '
   'division the model does not make. A layer''s identity is its name and nothing else, so '
   'there is no element to point at')
) AS s(element, superseded_by, no_such_fact, why)
